<title>USA: Delta starts JFK-Istanbul flights.</title>
<headline>Delta starts JFK-Istanbul flights.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines, said has begun a new nonstop daily service between New York's John F. Kennedy International Airport and Istanbul.</p>
<p>The service is operated by a Boeing 767-300ER and will offer up to ten tonnes per flight of cargo capacity. It formally started on May 6, an airline statement said.</p>
<p>The per kg cost of shipments exceeding 100 kg to Istanbul on Delta is $1.90 a kg, industry sources added. --Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
